###
# Logistics API Test Cases
# Base URL: http://localhost:8081
# Created: March 18, 2026

### ==================== ORDER ENDPOINTS ====================

### Test 1: Create Order - Standard Shipping to Canada and the expected cost should be 30.0 (12 * 2.5)
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "personA",
  "weight": 12,
  "shippingType": "STANDARD",
  "destination": "Canada"
}

### Test 2: Create Order - Express Shipping to Italy and the expected cost should be 18.75 ((5 * 2.5) * 1.5)
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "personB",
  "weight": 5,
  "shippingType": "EXPRESS",
  "destination": "Italy"
}

### Test 3: Create Order - Free Shipping to Africa (Should Succeed - Within Weight Limit which is 5kg) and the expected cost should be 0.0
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "personC",
  "weight": 3,
  "shippingType": "FREE",
  "destination": "Africa"
}

### Test 4: Create Order - Free Shipping to Germany (Should Fail - Exceeds Weight Limit) and the expected cost should be 0.0
POST http://localhost:8081/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerName": "personD",
  "weight":6,
  "shippingType": "FREE",
  "destination": "Germany"
}
### -----------------------------------------------------------------------END of Creation of orders -------------------------####

### ==================== VEHICLE ENDPOINTS ====================
##Van is always at service, while the truck and drone are not
## If we choose the van, the order will be dealyed and if we choose the truck or the drone, the order will be ready for delivery
### Test 6: Bind Van to Order - This should set the order status to DELAYED since the van is always at service
POST http://localhost:8081/vehicles/bindVehicleToOrder
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "VAN",
  "orderId": 1
}

### Test 7: Bind Truck to Order - This should set the order status to READY since the truck is not at service
POST http://localhost:8081/vehicles/bindVehicleToOrder
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "TRUCK",
  "orderId": 2
}

### Test 8: Bind Drone to Order - This should set the order status to READY since the drone is not at service
POST http://localhost:8081/vehicles/bindVehicleToOrder
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "type": "DRONE",
  "orderId": 3
}


